- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.KitStartTests`

**How to implement.** The start screen's state and its history messages, as a pure Elmish update over injected seams (001 §F 'The history list'; 001 §P StarKit, UnstarKit, ForgetKit and 'every user step is a semantic message'; the S5.2 brief: the messages are pure updates over a start-screen model, with the history and kit proxies injected; .spec-md §4 'UI'). New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartView.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.KitStartView`, compiled directly after `TableAndElementRotationView.fs` in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj`, because it reads `ConstructorMode` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:246`): one `<Compile>` line and no comment. Its module doc and every type, case and field doc are one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.2. It follows `LibraryWindowView.fs`: a context record of injected seams (`LibraryWindowView.fs:LibraryWindowContext`), a model, messages and an update that reaches IO only through the context (`LibraryWindowView.fs:updateLibraryWindow`). (1) `[<ReferenceEquality>] KitStartContext = { kitHistory : KitHistoryProxy; limit : KitHistoryLimit; clock : ClockProvider; author : KitAuthor; imports : CatalogueImportContext; picker : KitFolderPicker; showKit : OpenedKit -> unit }`: the kit history (step 165); its cap (step 162); the clock a bump reads; the author a new kit records (step 122); the library's import seam a kit's snapshot resolves against (step 94); the folder dialog of New kit…, Open kit… and Locate… (step 145); and the hand-off of an opened kit to the screen's window (step 179). This step's messages read `kitHistory` alone; step 177 reads the rest. (2) `KitStartOffer` = `NoKitStartOffer` | `MakeKitOffer of folder : KitFolder` (Open kit… met a folder without `.kit-json`) | `ReadOnlyKitOffer of folder : KitFolder * holder : KitLockHolder` (a kit open elsewhere, step 129): the question the screen asks after an open. (3) `KitRelocation = { missing : KitFolder; found : KitFolder }`: a missing kit's folder and the folder Locate… chose. (4) `KitStartModel = { context : KitStartContext; mode : ConstructorMode; history : KitHistory; filter : KitHistoryFilter; rows : KitHistoryRow list; offer : KitStartOffer; status : ControlCaption option }`: the constructor a chosen kit opens in (Main is `ForwardConstructor`, Inverse `InverseConstructor`); the history as last read or written; the filter's text; the listed rows, always `history.rowsMatching filter context.kitHistory.probeFolder` (step 170); the open question; and the last failure that needs telling. (5) `KitStartMsg`, in this step: `StarKit of KitFolder`, `UnstarKit of KitFolder`, `ForgetKit of KitFolder` (Remove from history), `LocateKit of KitRelocation` and `FilterKitHistory of KitHistoryFilter`; step 177 adds the open messages. (6) `initKitStart (context : KitStartContext) (mode : ConstructorMode) : KitStartModel` reads `context.kitHistory.readHistory ()` once and answers it with `KitHistoryFilter.none`, its rows, `NoKitStartOffer` and no status. (7) `updateKitStart (msg : KitStartMsg) (m : KitStartModel) : KitStartModel`: `StarKit f`, `UnstarKit f`, `ForgetKit f` and `LocateKit r` call `m.context.kitHistory.changeHistory` (step 171) with `star f`, `unstar f`, `forget f` and `relocate r.missing r.found` (steps 164, 171). `Ok history` answers the model holding that history, its rows recomputed and no status; `Error e` keeps the history and rows and sets `status` to `e.notSavedCaption`. `FilterKitHistory filter` holds the filter and recomputes the rows, writing nothing. Remove from history has no undo: the folder is untouched, and opening it again re-adds it (.spec-md §10.5). (8) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`: `type KitHistoryError with member this.notSavedCaption : ControlCaption` is `ControlCaption $"The kit history was not saved — {this.describe}"`, with a one-line doc. No view, window, cache, undo history or other message is added here. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/KitStartTests.fs`, `module KitStartTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment. Its fixture context holds a given `KitHistoryProxy`, `KitHistoryLimit.defaultValue`, a clock stepping one second per call from `DateTime(2026, 11, 3, 12, 0, 0, DateTimeKind.Utc)`, `KitAuthor "test"`, an import context over the Built-in library (`BuiltinCatalogue.freshStores ()`, step 94), a picker answering `None` and a `showKit` that records each kit it is given. Its history holds, in this stored order, unstarred `a` (12:05), starred `b` (12:01), unstarred `c` (12:09), starred `d` (12:07) and unstarred `e` (12:05), kit `x` named `Kit x` in `C:/kits/x` with a fixed GUID, written into `KitHistoryProxy.createInMemory` over the present folders `C:/kits/a`, `C:/kits/c`, `C:/kits/d` and `C:/kits/a2`. `the start screen opens on the history in display order, each row with its folder's presence`: `initKitStart` over that context and `ForwardConstructor` holds the stored history, `KitHistoryFilter.none`, rows `d`, `b`, `c`, `a`, `e` with `b` and `e` missing, `NoKitStartOffer`, no status and the mode. `starring, unstarring and forgetting a kit write the history and re-list it`: `StarKit` of `C:/kits/a` lists rows `d`, `a`, `b`, `c`, `e` and `readHistory ()` holds `a` starred; `UnstarKit` of it lists `d`, `b`, `c`, `a`, `e` again; `ForgetKit` of `C:/kits/b` removes `b` from the store and the rows. `locating a missing kit re-points its row and keeps its star`: `LocateKit { missing = C:/kits/b; found = C:/kits/a2 }` leaves `b`'s entry starred at `C:/kits/a2` and its row present. `the filter narrows the rows and writes nothing`: `FilterKitHistory (KitHistoryFilter "kit c")` lists `c` alone, `FilterKitHistory KitHistoryFilter.none` lists all five again, and `readHistory ()` is unchanged. `a history the store cannot write is shown and the rows are kept`: over a test-local proxy whose `writeHistory` answers `Error (KitHistoryWriteErr "disk full")`, `StarKit` keeps the rows and the history, sets a status containing `disk full`, and shows no kit.

**Acceptance.** After the start screen's model lands, `initKitStart` MUST list the history's rows in display order with their presence and `updateKitStart` MUST write StarKit, UnstarKit, ForgetKit and LocateKit through `changeHistory`, re-list the rows and show a failed write, and narrow the rows on FilterKitHistory writing nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the start screen opens on the history in display order, each row with its folder's presence`, `starring, unstarring and forgetting a kit write the history and re-list it`, `locating a missing kit re-points its row and keeps its star`, `the filter narrows the rows and writes nothing` and `a history the store cannot write is shown and the rows are kept`, the count rising by 5; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the fourteen s20 invariants MUST pass.
